# ── Why this file is not optional on Windows ────────────────────────────────
# core.autocrlf=true is set globally on the development machine, so without the rules
# below git checks these files out with CRLF endings. Three distinct failures follow, and
# none of them names line endings in its error message:
#
#   *.sh          `#!/usr/bin/env bash` becomes `...bash\r`, and the kernel looks for an
#                 interpreter literally called "bash\r":
#                     bash: ./scripts/bootstrap.sh: /usr/bin/env: bad interpreter
#
#   *.yaml        The worst of the three, because it survives all the way into the
#                 cluster. gitops/platform/localstack-wiring/cronjob.yaml carries a shell
#                 script inside a ConfigMap block scalar. CRLF in the YAML puts a carriage
#                 return at the end of every line of that script, so the in-cluster `sh`
#                 sees `set -eu\r` and `fi\r`. Same for every Tekton `script:` block. YAML
#                 itself parses fine, which is what makes it hard to find.
#
#   .env          Sourced by scripts/lib.sh. `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1\r` reaches the
#                 AWS CLI as an invalid region. lib.sh strips CR defensively for exactly
#                 this reason, but the fix belongs here as well as there.
#
# `text eol=lf` means: normalise to LF in the repository AND check out as LF regardless of
# core.autocrlf. Editors on Windows handle LF fine; the shells and parsers above do not
# handle CRLF at all.
#
# After adding this file, existing entries in the index still hold CRLF. Renormalise once:
#     git add --renormalize .
* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
.env        text eol=lf
.env.*      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf

# Binaries LocalStack caches under ./data are gitignored, but be explicit in case the
# ignore rule is ever relaxed.
*.png       binary
*.svg       text eol=lf
*.avro      binary
*.pem       text eol=lf
*.crt       text eol=lf
